<p>(a) In fiscal 1997, the company's Healthcare Information Systems business was transferred from the medical electronic equipment and service grouping to the computer products, service and support grouping.  Fiscal 1996 orders and net revenue have been restated to be consistent with the new presentation.  The change did not affect the company's total orders or net revenue.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610  </p>
<p>Note: Analysts estimates for the quarter was $0.68 per share, according to First Call.</p>
<p>Net revenue in the United States was $4.8 billion, an increase of 15 percent compared with a year ago, while revenue from outside the United States also rose 15 percent to $5.7 billion.</p>
<p>In Europe, orders totaled $3.1 billion, up 13 percent in dollars and 22 percent in local currency.  In Asia Pacific, Canada and Latin America, orders increased 18 percent to $2.4 billion. Currency effects reduced the company's order growth by about 5 percentage points.</p>
<p>Net revenue in the computer business increased 17 percent over last year's third quarter and totaled $8.7 billion. Orders in the computer business rose 20 percent over the same period last year and were $8.4 billion.</p>
